-- title:
--   Descent along an isogeny of formal groups: local Noetherian base
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a local Noetherian commutative ring, $n$ a natural number, and let $F,F'$ be $n$-dimensional formal group laws over $B$: each is given by an $n$-tuple of power series in the $2n$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$, with vanishing constant terms, with the coefficient of $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}$ and of $X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$ in the $i$-th component equal to $1$ if $i=j$ and $0$ otherwise, and satisfying the associativity identity; both are assumed commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $\rho = (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ be an $n$-tuple in $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ with $\rho_i(0)=0$ and $\rho(F(x,y)) = F'(\rho(x),\rho(y))$ componentwise (substitution of $F$ into $\rho_i$ equals substitution of $\rho$ in the $\mathrm{inl}$ variables and $\rho$ in the $\mathrm{inr}$ variables into the $i$-th component of $F'$). Assume some power $X_i^N$ of each variable lies in the ideal $(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$, and that $B[\![x]\!]/(\rho)$ is finite and projective as a $B$-module. Then for every $G \in B[\![x]\!]$ such that $G(F(x,y)) - G(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by $\rho_1(y),\dots,\rho_n(y)$, there is $H \in B[\![x]\!]$ with $G = H(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ and $H(0)=G(0)$.
--
--   This is the descent statement for an isogeny $\rho : F \to F'$ of commutative formal group laws with finite projective kernel algebra: a power series invariant under translation by the kernel is a power series in the coordinates of $\rho$. It is the local Noetherian case, from which the version over a general Noetherian base, [`MvFormalGroup.exists_eq_subst_of_subst_toPowerSeries_sub_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_eq_subst_of_subst_toPowerSeries_sub_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span), is obtained; the proof uses the existence and uniqueness of expansions of elements of $B[\![x]\!]$ over $B[\![u]\!]$ along $\rho$ in a basis lifting a residue-field basis of the kernel algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_eq_subst_of_subst_toPowerSeries_sub_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span_of_isLocalRing.lean

